#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:3 1eff706a26a0412a99bba0a399256bfe
msgid "Privacy policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:6 557d9d02bfd041318ce6f4140d4be43e
msgid ""
"The short version is that we try to respect your privacy as much as "
"possible. We absolutely do not sell any user data. In fact, we go out of our "
"way to help you keep your data private from everyone, including us. For "
"example, from the moment you :doc:`install Qubes OS </user/downloading-"
"installing-upgrading/installation-guide>`, we offer to set up `Whonix "
"<https://www.whonix.org/>`__ so that all of your updates are routed through "
"`Tor <https://www.torproject.org/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:9 a13a2db7860d493499cc7e7b1e36509b
msgid "Website"
msgstr "網站"

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:12 29dd3bf0f2334e189537a1b6df5844f1
msgid ""
"For the legally-required boilerplate, see `Website Privacy Policy <https://"
"www.qubes-os.org/website-privacy-policy/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:14 8518bf451f73467cb2428301a397ff51
msgid ""
"This is just a static website generated with Jekyll and hosted from GitHub "
"Pages. We try to use as little JavaScript as possible. We host all resources "
"locally (no third-party CDNs) so that you only have to connect to one "
"domain. The website should be easy to browse using Tor Browser and with "
"scripts blocked. We also have an `onion service <http://"
"qubesosfasa4zl44o4tws22di6kepyzfeqv3tg4e3ztknltfxqrymdad.onion/>`__ (access "
"is not logged). We even go out of our way to make it easy to download `this "
"website’s git repo <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubesos.github.io>`__, "
"including all the website source code, so that you can host this entire site "
"from your own local machine offline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:16 94651ab9c96a48f9a9e87af4a7b5b9b1
msgid ""
"Most of the website is written in Markdown so that the plain text can be "
"enjoyed from the comfort of your terminal. Obviously, we don’t use any ads "
"or trackers, but this is still a public website, so man-in-the-middle "
"attacks and such are always a possibility. Please be careful. See :ref:`FAQ: "
"Should I trust this website? <introduction/faq:should i trust this website?>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:20 099a81d95699489787174cb3172919ae
msgid "Qubes OS documentation"
msgstr "Qubes OS 文件"

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:22 e15a2a3e212a4f828d0b158a038a263d
msgid ""
"Qubes OS documentation is hosted on `Read The Docs <https://about."
"readthedocs.com/>`__. We’ve converted all of the :doc:`documentation </"
"index>` from Markdown to reStructuredText. You can enjoy the plain text from "
"the comfort of your terminal. Here’s the `repo <https://github.com/QubesOS/"
"qubes-doc>`__. (By the way, Git tags on our repos are PGP-signed so you can :"
"doc:`verify </project-security/verifying-signatures>` the authenticity of "
"the content.) We omit the ethical ads from RTD, but this is still a public "
"website, so man-in-the-middle attacks and such are always a possibility. "
"Please be careful. Also see :ref:`FAQ: Why is the documentation hosted on "
"ReadTheDocs as opposed to the website? <introduction/faq:why is the "
"documentation hosted on readthedocs as opposed to the website?>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:25 cb5135d0f5bf41d281ea0f11aba32b25
msgid ""
"Please refer to RTD's `privacy policy <https://docs.readthedocs.com/platform/"
"stable/privacy-policy.html>`__ for more information. As per RTD site, the TL;"
"DR version is as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:36 422cb78a27434f79a40079357177909c
msgid "Update Servers and Repositories"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:39 9c121e3828d445279bb5137805c9ed9a
msgid ""
"We provide repositories at https://yum.qubes-os.org and https://deb.qubes-os."
"org."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:41 da009c2da228491596646858bf56587b
msgid ""
"We collect and store standard server access and error logs, which include IP "
"addresses. We use this data for generating :doc:`Qubes userbase statistics </"
"introduction/statistics>` and for incident response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:43 5efa4a92572b42ada8264983a72df4ae
msgid ""
"The data is retained for up to three months so that we can re-calculate the "
"previous two months’ statistics in case anything goes wrong. After that, the "
"data is deleted. We never sell the data to anyone or share it with any third "
"party."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:45 d55beacb1246448f82b873b5e6804c29
msgid ""
"If you would like to hide your IP address from us, we strongly encourage it "
"and are happy to help you do so! Simply choose the Whonix option to route "
"all of your updates over Tor when :doc:`installing Qubes OS </user/"
"downloading-installing-upgrading/installation-guide>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:48 45e688b09a3d4fa8810d7e8b83bd5f08
msgid "Onion Services"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:51 b93f137d6f74472cb070c364f185fd06
msgid ""
"We provide an `onion service <http://www."
"qubesosfasa4zl44o4tws22di6kepyzfeqv3tg4e3ztknltfxqrymdad.onion>`__ for the "
"website and onion service mirrors of the repositories. Access to these "
"servers is not logged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:54 29fef792e5174c3383866660c221c0e8
msgid "Mirrors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:57 a3dc9cc149e34fe4abc4c13023ef4a4d
msgid ""
"There are also other third-party mirrors hosted by volunteers. These are "
"used both for `ISO downloads <https://www.qubes-os.org/downloads/"
"#mirrors>`__ and :ref:`updates <introduction/privacy:update servers and "
"repositories>`. We have no control over what data these mirrors collect or "
"with whom they share it. Please see the privacy policy of each respective "
"mirror operator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:60 77a7a36c03b643f2bdb3e2ba0351a935
msgid "Qubes OS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:63 edfe44b58ba94256a1f8875be55bf48e
msgid ""
"We have specifically designed Qubes OS so that it is not possible to collect "
"any data directly from Qubes OS installations. In other words, Qubes OS does "
"not have the ability to “phone home” and is intentionally architected to "
"forbid that from happening. This is mainly because we have ensured that dom0 "
"has no network access."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:65 e5eb8df5bac3414da5fd1b559dbd00ae
msgid ""
"We don’t want the ability to collect any data directly from Qubes OS "
"installations, because if anyone has that power, then the system is not "
"secure. We use Qubes OS ourselves as a daily driver for our work and "
"personal lives, so our interests are aligned with yours. We want privacy "
"too! Thankfully, Qubes OS is free and open-source software, so you don’t "
"have to take our word for it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:67 051e13bff72f46dc8a8dbf1cf6de1b4d
msgid ""
"Of course, third-party software (including other operating systems) running "
"inside of Qubes OS may not be as privacy-respecting, so please be mindful of "
"what you install. We have no control over such third-party software."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../introduction/privacy.rst:69 c1461bbd7a714b30aea60c8ba81c3d5b
msgid ""
"For more information, please see :ref:`FAQ: How does Qubes OS provide "
"privacy? <introduction/faq:how does qubes os provide privacy?>`"
msgstr ""
